WEBVTT

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.610
What's going on?!

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.150
The tower! This tower is becoming Galatea!

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.760
We can't stay here any longer!

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.320
The tower? Becoming Galatea?

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.760
Damn! Is there any way we can win?!

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.160
How is Sylia?

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.170
She's been like that for a while now.

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:14.010
Mackey...

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.380
I'm sure he'll regain his memories.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.790
Mackey was so human.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:21.320
I'm sure he keeps the memory
of you somewhere, Nene.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.220
Thanks, Linna.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.190
Is this the end for us?

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.490
I won't let it end!

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.990
Bring the toolbox over there.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:46.810
Nigel...

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.180
I don't care whether you ride or not.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.240
This is the only thing I can do now.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:55.110
Please stay with Sylia.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.720
Sylia needs you now.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.310
I see!

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.900
How about this then?

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:20.870
Come on, come on, come on!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.780
I did it! What a genius I am!

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:31.810
Galatea...

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:33.690
What is this?

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:38.100
This? The view from a NSA spy satellite.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.670
What an accomplishment!

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:43.570
Look, Galatea is heading toward
the core of the Umbrella.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.040
Umbrella?

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.110
It's the Showhamm Project.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:50.740
However, the person who created
it isn't with us any longer.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.710
Galatea intends to inherit it
for a different purpose.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.550
A different purpose?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.620
The Showhamm Project was a
plan to accumulate solar power

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.260
in the underground Dragon Line,

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.090
by collecting pure sunlight
outside of the atmosphere

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.220
and sending it to the Genom Tower as beams.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.330
It was all over the news.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:16.200
I didn't have any interest in stuff like that.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.170
The Dragon Lines in Tokyo
have become boomers.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:23.180
Right. We already cut them up inside Tokyo.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:26.170
However, if the stronger
phenomenon flows into it...

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.850
Does she intend to irradiate the
phenomenon from space?!

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.290
It's the most effective way to do it, isn't it?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.190
Effective for what?

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.380
To turn all machines on Earth into boomers.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.390
Wait a second.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.160
What?!

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.870
You said this is the picture from
an NSA satellite, didn't you?!

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.030
Yes.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.830
A shuttle missile.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.010
I can't believe they'd use a nuclear weapon.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.000
Nuclear?!

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.760
The missiles were turned into boomers.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.680
Every country is starting to panic.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.550
They're all afraid of their countries
becoming just like Tokyo.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.420
Of course they are.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:43.720
But if they find out that Galatea is
going to take over Showhamm,

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.260
there would be one really bad thing.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:46.530
What's that?

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:49.660
Destroy the beam's reception unit.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.720
A nuclear attack on Tokyo.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.600
I'm going after Galatea! I'll catch and smash her!

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.070
I've been thinking about getting
away from the city for a while.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:12.240
We'd been having fun, feeling good,

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:16.540
we killed mad boomers and
earned some money.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.250
We didn't want to feel sad.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.600
Sometimes circumstances
force you to do things.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.710
The woman you fall in love
with loves somebody else,

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:37.110
but you would hate yourself
if you gave up on her.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:45.040
Therefore, if I can, I want to
be with you until the end.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:51.520
I wish Sylia designed hard suits for men.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:56.260
I'm not a transvestite, but I would
not mind dressing up like you.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:00.760
Shut up.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.150
Those two fit well, don't they?

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:19.050
I don't know. I'm sure a man like
Leon-pea is the henpecked type.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.250
I guess you're right!

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.920
Two more hours...

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:31.360
How long have you been there?!

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.370
What? We were the first ones here.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:37.100
You didn't see us at all, did you?

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.540
I understand.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:42.770
Shut up! Well, did you find
a way to chase Galatea?

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.950
Are we going to use the rocket
located at Tanegashima Island?

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:49.550
There's no way we'd be able
to launch it by ourselves.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.650
Instead, I found a better route

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:54.710
which is surer and we'll be able to
arrive there earlier than Galatea.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.680
Sylia, we're going after Galatea.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.780
You know, I appreciate you, Sylia,

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:26.810
so I'll do whatever I can for you.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.480
Please take care of Mackey!

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.990
We promise we'll come back.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.090
I'm sure Mackey will remember you, Sylia.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.560
Of course, he'll remember me too.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.230
It's so quiet, isn't it?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.500
Do you want to know the reason?

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:58.220
The reason why I've always hated the AD Police.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:02.420
A long time ago, a mad boomer
came to the place where I lived,

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.430
a site which used to be a factory.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.550
Then we showed up, didn't we?

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.490
Did we miss the target then?

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:15.670
You got it. An armored car even
plowed into the place,

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:18.570
and fired a ton of bullets that
piled up like a mountain.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:19.730
Well...

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.740
Oh, you were injured at that time, weren't you?

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.540
I ran away, but

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:29.880
one of the disks that I treasured was burned.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.150
Disk?

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.350
My favorite song.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:35.020
I'd been hoping that some day,

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:37.650
I'd be able to sing it in front of a
huge crowd at Wembley Stadium.

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.920
For a reason like that...

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:51.340
The skyhook comes alongside the platform
just off of Boso peninsula, right?

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:55.040
But the skyhook is just for cargo.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.840
Yes, so we'll get in with the cargo
before the pallet starts moving.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:04.120
The skyhook will grab the
cargo which we're in and...

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.140
Fly us into space!

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:30.130
Sing.

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:36.640
The song you wanted to sing. I'm the audience.

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:49.430
Sadness, pain and struggle

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:58.500
They're overflowing and I can't
hold them in my arms

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:12.480
Rather than accepting a fate
like this and giving up

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:24.460
I believe in my power to make them change, so

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:31.300
I will keep walking

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:38.410
Hey, the slider pallet is already moving!

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.640
It can't be!

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:46.110
We have more than an hour
until the skyhook arrives.

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:48.420
Oh, my God!

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.080
Priss, what'll we do?!

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.050
Oh, no...

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.960
The supplier pallet!

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.830
The receiver pallet too!

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.570
This place has been affected
by the phenomenon.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:14.880
Priss, what'll we do?

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:19.450
Even if there's no pallet, the
skyhook will come on time.

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.580
Even if it comes, it won't stop for you.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:40.800
When the skyhook passes the
platform, its speed is 780km/hour!

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:46.380
That's it. We don't have any other way, do we?

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.810
Hurry up and get out of here!

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:59.290
What are you doing? Hurry up!

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:10.290
I...

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:14.970
I don't care if the entire Earth
becomes a boomer,

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:19.310
just promise me you'll make
it back alive. All of you!

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:29.560
I wonder why Leon-pyon couldn't
say something nicer than that?

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:31.790
I think that was him at his best.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.350
Hold on tight!

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.290
Go!

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:00.450
Roger!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.480
Okay.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.450
Rock n' roll!

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.300
You two are pretty heavy.

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:20.870
Priss, you're talking about
our hard suits, aren't you?!

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:25.010
Yeah...

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.360
It's huge!

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.630
It's coming, it's coming!

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:56.430
Faster, faster!

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.210
Motoslave, you're a boomer too, aren't you?

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:03.650
Show us what you've got!

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:16.560
We did it! We're going into space!

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.150
Let's fly into space!

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.200
NOW!

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:23.030
Linna, thrust your jets!

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.540
Linna! Linna!

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:04.730
Am I alive?

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:06.750
And you, Nene?

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.680
I'm alive!

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:15.350
The Knight Sabers are going into space, right?

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:18.420
We should move to the other block.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:21.230
Even though our hard suits can
generate oxygen internally,

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:23.590
it won't last forever.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:25.000
Can you stand up?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:25.230
Yes, I'm fine.
Can you stand up?

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.720
Yes, I'm fine.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.540
Wait!

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:42.880
Nobody is allowed to ride this
shuttle without special permission.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:47.110
Excuse me, but I have to report
this to the operation center.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.960
This boomer looks fine, doesn't it?

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:53.760
Well, so far it's still a boomer
well disposed to humans.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:56.460
But the true character of the
boomer is Galatea, you know.

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:02.370
Hello, Mr. Boomer. We have tickets, of course.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:06.540
Oh, I see. My apologies.

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:10.210
Well, please relax and enjoy
the journey into space.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.400
As if I believed THAT!

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:17.350
Mr. Boomer, I don't think there's
anyone in the operation center

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.990
to receive your report, is there?

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.550
You're absolutely right.

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:24.420
I haven't been able to contact them for a week,

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:27.690
so I haven't be able to accomplish my mission.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.330
Then, I will give you a new mission.

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:32.760
Yes, Ma'am. What is it?

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:38.000
The stars look strange. They
aren't twinkling, are they?

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:41.240
There's no atmosphere, so of course they don't.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:45.310
You aren't even impressed by the
fact that we're in space, are you?

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:46.400
I guess not.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:48.310
Space?

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:52.470
I wanted to become an astronaut
when I was a kid.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:58.820
But why didn't you? You could
have since you're so smart, right?

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:01.160
I was a little too short.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.990
I was so disappointed when I read
the official NASDA regulations.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:08.670
But now your dream came true, so it worked out.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:11.400
I guess. Just like you, Linna?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.370
What? Me?

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:17.640
In my case, my dream was
to join the Knight Sabers,

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:21.670
but I didn't expect that I'd
come this far into space!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:26.050
Where's Priss?

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:28.080
Where?

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:34.960
You did a good job.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:39.290
Even though you look like a bike,
you're a boomer, right? Sorry.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:45.090
I hated to ride you at the
beginning, just like this hard suit.

00:18:46.010 --> 00:18:48.510
But if we communicated with
each other with our hearts,

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:52.950
boomers wouldn't have become
monsters like Galatea,

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.850
and they might have been able
to become our friends.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:03.720
It might be selfish to think this way.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:06.250
I'm thinking about boomers
in my favorite way, aren't I?

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:16.560
Thanks...

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:31.510
Four more hours until we arrive at the Umbrella.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.590
Where's Galatea?

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.290
Be patient for a little while, please.

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.480
Yes, Ma'am.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:38.350
Here you go.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:45.860
We should be thankful to the
chairman of Genom for one thing,

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:48.130
that he didn't put rocket engines
in the Genom Tower.

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:50.960
We'll be able to arrive before Galatea, won't we?

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:54.130
If we don't, we have no idea what will happen.

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:56.140
That's true.

00:19:56.140 --> 00:20:02.080
Excuse me, but who is Galatea?
A new manager of boomers?

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:05.310
Well, something like that, I guess.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:10.480
But she's trying to control the Earth like a god.

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:48.820
So many stars.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:55.330
How beautiful! So many stars filling the sky.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:59.760
Next Episode

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.310
Finally, we arrive at the Umbrella

00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:05.880
which is the key to the Showhamm Project, but...

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:08.650
by that time, the place had
become Galatea's evil castle.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:13.020
Boomer eggs are propagating as if
they were the focus of a disease.

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:16.530
Then, our shadows of light appear.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:19.000
What is Galatea thinking of doing?!

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:21.330
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
